19:["$","p","3",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Codes run from three to seven characters, and a decimal point follows the third character. Crucially, a three-character code is only billable when no further subdivision exists for it. Most three-character entries are category headers, and submitting one where subdivisions exist produces exactly the rejection above."}]
1a:["$","div","4",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-primary-200 bg-primary-50/50 p-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-700 mb-2","children":"Worked example"}],["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1","children":"Building a complete fracture code"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"Code a follow-up visit for a patient with a healing displaced fracture of the distal end of the left radius."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":1}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Start with the category: S52 covers fracture of the forearm."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"S-codes cover injuries by body region, and S52 narrows to the forearm. This is the category, not a billable code — building outward from the category is how you make sure you have not skipped a level of specificity."}]]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":2}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Add characters for the specific site and fracture type."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"The distal radius has its own subdivision, and within it, codes separate displaced from non-displaced fractures. The documentation says displaced, so that branch is chosen. Where documentation does not specify, the coding guidelines direct that a fracture not indicated as displaced or non-displaced is coded as displaced."}]]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":3}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Add laterality: left."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"The radius exists on both sides, so ICD-10-CM provides separate codes for right and left. The note documents left, so an unspecified-side code would be wrong and would likely be denied."}]]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":4}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Add the 7th character for the encounter type."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"This is a follow-up during healing, so the extension for a subsequent encounter with routine healing applies — not the initial-encounter extension. The 7th character is what distinguishes the first visit for the injury from every visit afterwards, and choosing it wrongly changes the clinical meaning of the claim entirely."}]]}]]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":5}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Check the character count and insert the placeholder X if needed."}],"$L20"]}]]}]]}],"$L21","$L22"]}]
1b:["$","div","1",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"The placeholder X and the 7th character"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Two features of ICD-10-CM confuse most newcomers, and both concern the tail of the code."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"The placeholder X fills empty character positions so that a required 7th character lands in the 7th position. It carries no meaning of its own; it is purely positional. If a code needs a 7th character but only has four meaningful characters, X is inserted twice to pad positions five and six."}],["$","figure","2",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Extension"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Means"}],["$","th","2",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Use for"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"A"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Initial encounter"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"While the patient is receiving active treatment for the injury"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"D"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Subsequent encounter"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Routine care during the healing or recovery phase"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"S"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Sequela"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"A complication or condition arising as a direct result of the injury"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Common 7th character extensions for injuries"}]]}],["$","div","3",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"Initial encounter does not mean the first visit. It means the patient is receiving active treatment for the injury — which can span several visits, and can include a first visit to a new provider. Subsequent encounter means routine healing care. This is one of the most commonly miscoded elements in ICD-10-CM, precisely because the everyday meaning of 'initial' is not the coding meaning."]}],["$","$L23","4",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"A patient is seen for the third time for a healing ankle fracture. No new treatment is provided; the provider checks healing progress. Which 7th character applies?","options":["A, because the fracture is still the reason for the visit","D, because this is routine care during the healing phase","S, because the fracture is an ongoing problem","No 7th character is needed for follow-up visits"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"D indicates a subsequent encounter — routine care while the injury heals, with no active treatment being provided. A would apply during active treatment, and S is reserved for a sequela, meaning a lasting condition resulting from the injury rather than the injury itself.","optionRationales":["A is for active treatment of the injury, not for monitoring healing progress.","Correct. Routine care during the healing phase is a subsequent encounter, extension D.","S is for a sequela — a late effect such as a resulting deformity — not for an injury that is still healing normally.","The 7th character is required for these injury codes at every encounter. Omitting it produces an invalid code."]}}]]}]]}]
1c:["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl","children":"Apply what you've learned in this lesson."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"You will need access to a current ICD-10-CM code set. Free searchable versions are published by CMS."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Look up the category for type 2 diabetes mellitus. List three subdivisions that differ by complication, and note what documentation would be needed to choose between them."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Find a code that requires a 7th character and has fewer than six meaningful characters. Write it out with the placeholder X in the correct positions."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"For a patient seen for a laceration of the right index finger without damage to the nail, find the most specific code available and note every axis of specificity you had to satisfy."}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Explain in three sentences why a payer might deny an unspecified-laterality code even though the code is valid."}]]}]]}]}]]}]
